{"name":"Badlands Taupe","hex":"#d5bcb3","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"badlands","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An arid terrain characterized by severe erosion of sedimentary rocks.","An arid region of Western Canada characterized by significant erosion and odd land formations containing dinosaur and other fossils."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/badlands"},{"term":"taupe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dark brownish-grey colour, the colour of moleskin."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark brownish-grey colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/taupe"}],"entries":[{"title":"Badlands","blocks":[{"text":"Badlands are a type of dry terrain where softer sedimentary rocks and clay-rich soils have been extensively eroded. They are characterized by steep slopes, minimal vegetation, lack of a substantial regolith, and high drainage density. Ravines, gullies, buttes, hoodoos and other such geologic forms are common in badlands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Chinle_Badlands.jpg/330px-Chinle_Badlands.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Badlands","wikidata":"Q272921"},{"title":"Taupe","blocks":[{"text":"Taupe is a dark gray-brown color. The word derives from the French noun taupe meaning \"mole\". The name originally referred only to the average color of the French mole, but beginning in the 1940s, its usage expanded to encompass a wider range of shades."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taupe","wikidata":"Q2307593"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/A030%2C_Theodore_Roosevelt_National_Park%2C_North_Dakota%2C_USA%2C_2001.jpg/330px-A030%2C_Theodore_Roosevelt_National_Park%2C_North_Dakota%2C_USA%2C_2001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.or